/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050098 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "2d131eff-4143-5f33-ab1b-d2795c01303f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050309 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050309 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050309 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050309 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050309 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050309 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050309 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs With Complex Eigenvalues" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050309 #edb/ref 1033 2819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050309 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "3ece60c2-2440-5884-ade0-5ec738e1db78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186229166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186229167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186229168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs With Sinusoidal Forcing" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1033 6680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050392 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "45561e84-38ff-5ce1-9f3c-76fdda09730b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050450 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050450 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050450 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050450 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050450 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050450 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs With Repeated Eigenvalues" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050450 #edb/ref 1033 2818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050450 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "49ef522d-8ba6-502a-8a64-c19ff9a6b681" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050801 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050801 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050801 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050801 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050801 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050801 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050801 #edb/ref 1033 3189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050801 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "68086256-0558-57ff-bb09-7a45eb02cfce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166520 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21540" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166520 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](images/ea/eaf224db946e02695b83465fa548948a27e7587c7d4b270c604c897cdd4a2228.png)\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](images/b7/b7ae867ae694152125bc8cdf1ee7ab34c52b0c050408db3d2da86c7cbbc88493.png)\nFind the general solution of the system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166520 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c5e60742-2571-5100-96be-a7578e6dda07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166520 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\mathbf{x}_c(t) + \\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](images/c6/c68bfa253f23fb2c116b8769744e6fd22b7b898047e3ef3fe97f66dd91fefaa1.png)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n![](images/b2/b270d56283fdced6971e1a00fc3e642e379fc9348a0e4fb17a97ba6db2d8fc13.png)\nwhere $a,b$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of $\\mathbf{x}_p$ with respect to $t$ gives\n![](images/ca/ca497159ae72a8b87997c78815119bb3de53782878cb2209072dcc505c902f37.png)\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute $\\mathbf{x}_p$ and $\\mathbf{x}'_p$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 7[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a+b \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7a \\\\ 7b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1 \\\\ b-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3a+b-1=7a \\\\ b-3=7b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nb - 7b = 3\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\nb = -\\dfrac12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n3a - \\dfrac12 - 1 = 7a\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\na = -\\dfrac38.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n![](images/ff/fff596d40155dc7787910405557a722b5258890e3fae88f60842de92fac47177.png)\n\nAnd thus, the general solution is given by\n![](images/dc/dc74c06c84905f8490932369e24cecd8f3b7eb64fdc4413e42c2f8bc1a3f3cbd.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166521 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21541" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166521 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/5b/5b0bb8069abe99949fc52c0be82c22f5879d7ca0ac334af396f47efa41ae0b5e.png)\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n![](images/f2/f220005265275c9297b7beef58777203a94351cb4957a26ca630802664759dc5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166521 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6f03c3e2-26dc-5ef3-90d9-9b80feac1ad4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166521 #edb/ref 1074 "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n![](images/40/40f93d12ebe4519dc4aa15f0df4b568ffa25f25afd99ec45130b569083c21fe0.png)\nwhere $c_1,c_2$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2.$ Substituting $t = 0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\ {e}^{0}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-0+4 \\\\ -{0}^{2}+2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+4 \\\\ {c}_{2}+2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+4=6 \\\\ {c}_{2}+2=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $c_1 = 2.$ From the second equation, we have $c_2 = -1.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n![](images/94/948088eb5d495f3d8a8a96f038b5b036b53fa398544f9faedbb08026e96b661e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166522 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21543" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166522 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n![](images/c9/c9810bd07c9da4bd3d803740a85ce484cd92f4a0d8cb73af75d53602f8611a72.png)\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n![](images/85/85139452af923a4f7b793fc47454cb99579ce0fa68ae33de3a15747501f624ef.png)\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\mathbf{x}_c(t)+\\mathbf{x}_p(t),$ where $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution $\\mathbf{x}_p(t).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166522 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a5c44ae4-e55b-512f-ac1c-46f62950c1f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166522 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\mathbf{x}_c(t)+\\mathbf{x}_p(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_c(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and $\\mathbf{x}_p(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n![](images/13/13785393b66b769c10efcbf7cf9f1bb4f05c412a1ddb8649427b659728c7bd3e.png)\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is sinusoidal. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal, i.e.\n![](images/4b/4b2dbbf0847dc9ea9f438e3848dca79da5f4e3f4473ab325a5f2c48e8b77e98c.png)\nwhere $a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2$ are constants that are to be determined." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166523 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21544" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166523 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+4{t}^{2}+t-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{t}^{2}+5t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite the system of linear ODEs in matrix form." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166523 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aabc0f35-fdfc-573a-8d86-ada823a380a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166523 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=(-2)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+4\\cdot {t}^{2}+1\\cdot t+(-2) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+0\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {t}^{2}+5\\cdot t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix 