edb/ref 17592186304484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305062 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305062 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305062 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305062 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305062 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332584" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305062 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305062 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  | $\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} |  | $\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |  | {{field-7}} |  |  | {{field-8}} |  |  |  |  |  |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305062 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "72939cc6-3d0d-529a-9c8c-72658e0c2def" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305062 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+(-5)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=(-1)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+1\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305112 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305112 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332749" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305112 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305112 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{7}{5}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}(t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]){e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305112 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "24c639b5-3938-594c-bf24-83bf8b532823" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305112 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also constant, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
